//@version=6
// =====================================================================================
// OPENING-RANGE BREAKOUT -- STRATEGY  ("Sapporo")
//
// Trades the break of the US cash RTH opening range. Grounded in docs/rth_open_pierce_stats.md
// (5yr MNQ): the 08:30-09:00 CT open range is ~102 pt median (~5x the overnight window), opens
// COMMIT to one direction (both bands pierced same-open only 4% of days), and the open window is
// only ~1/3 of the full-day range -- a break at the open is the opening leg of a big-range day.
// So: define the range, trade the break, ride the day's direction, flat by EOD (no overnight).
//
//   RANGE : high/low of the first orMinutes after RTH open (08:30 CT / 14:30 LDN). One box/day.
//   ENTRY : first bar that CLOSES beyond OR-high+buffer (long) or OR-low-buffer (short). One
//           trade per day per side. Break window closes at breakEndMin (no chasing a late break).
//   SLOPE ROUTER (optional, the doc's one monotonic filter, section 11): only take the break when
//           the slope into it is steep enough (steep up-slope = runaway; flat/neg = reverts). Skips
//           the limp breaks that revert. Router is OFF by default -- prove the baseline first.
//   OR-SIZE FILTER (optional): only take the break when the OR width is >= orMinPts (tiny OR = no
//           conviction). Vol-relative sizing left to the port sweep.
//   REL-VOL DAY GATE (optional, OFF by default): skip the day entirely unless its opening-range
//           volume is LOW vs its own recent baseline. Inverted vs the equity ORB literature -- see
//           the input block below for the numbers and the caveat.
//   EXIT  : one of {trailing stop, fixed TP+SL, OR-width targets, pure EOD hold} -- exitMode picks
//           one. The docs say exit choice is likely the whole game; sweep it on this one engine.
//   EOD   : flatten at session close (15:00 CT / 21:00 LDN). No overnight carry.
//
// UNVALIDATED. This file exists to get an honest 5yr-vs-OOS number at 1pt slip, exTop10, per-year,
// long/short split. Do NOT claim an edge before the port chain agrees and the cost gate is cleared.
// =====================================================================================
strategy("Opening-Range Breakout Strategy", overlay=true, max_labels_count=500, max_bars_back=5000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1, initial_capital=100000,
     calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=true, slippage=0)

//=============================
// Inputs -- opening range definition
//=============================
orMinutes   = input.int(30,   "Opening-range length (min after RTH open)", minval=1, maxval=120, group="Opening range")
breakEndMin = input.int(120,  "Break window ends this many min after open (no entry after)", minval=1, maxval=390, group="Opening range")
breakBuf    = input.float(3.0, "Breakout buffer beyond OR edge (pts)", minval=0.0, step=0.5, group="Opening range")
orMinPts    = input.float(0.0, "OR-size filter: only trade if OR width >= this (pts, 0 = off)", minval=0.0, step=5.0, group="Opening range")

//=============================
// Inputs -- side
//=============================
enableLong  = input.bool(true, "Take LONG breaks (break of OR high)",  group="Side")
enableShort = input.bool(true, "Take SHORT breaks (break of OR low)",  group="Side")

//=============================
// Inputs -- slope router (docs/rth_open_pierce_stats.md section 11: slope at pierce separates
// runaways (steep) from reverters (flat/neg). Take the break only if the slope into it is steep
// enough in the break direction. slopeLen bars of simple net slope (pts/bar). OFF by default.
//=============================
useSlopeRouter = input.bool(false, "Slope router: require steep slope into the break", group="Slope router")
slopeLen    = input.int(15,   "Slope window (bars into the break)", minval=2, maxval=120, group="Slope router")
slopeMinPB  = input.float(1.0, "Min slope magnitude to take the break (pts/bar)", minval=0.0, step=0.25, group="Slope router")

//=============================
// Inputs -- TRAILING-30 CVD GATE (optional). Order-flow direction filter. From the 2025 Databento
// trades-schema study (docs/orderflow_2025_test_plan.md): breaks whose trailing-30-min cumulative
// volume delta runs HARD AGAINST the break direction are a clean loser bucket (removed 27 trades
// averaging -120pt, 22% win, at the strong-disagreement threshold). Take the break only unless the
// trailing-CVD opposes it by more than cvdThresh. CVD here is built from real aggressor up/down
// volume via request.security_lower_tf (seconds bars) -- needs a data feed that provides it (CME
// real-time on Premium does). OFF by default -- prove the baseline first; recalibrate cvdThresh on
// the live TV delta scale (the study's 2000 was Databento contract-units, does NOT transfer).
//   thresh=0 -> plain SIGN gate (skip any break the flow opposes).
//   thresh>0 -> only skip breaks the flow opposes by MORE than thresh (the study's sweet spot).
//=============================
//=============================
// Inputs -- RELATIVE-VOLUME DAY GATE (optional). Trade only days whose OPENING-RANGE volume is
// low relative to its own recent history. rv = (volume inside today's OR window) / (mean OR-window
// volume of the previous rvDays ACTIVE days). Take the break only when rv <= rvMax.
//
// NOTE THE SIGN -- this is INVERTED vs the equity ORB literature. Zarattini et al's "Stocks in Play"
// filter trades the HIGH relative-volume names; on MNQ that loses (rv>=1.0 -> -964 net, 2/6 yrs;
// rv>=1.1 -> -4,629 and 0/6 yrs). The LOW-rel-vol side is what pays here (5yr @1pt slip):
//   baseline (gate off)  +7,970  exTop10 +1,314  PF 1.13  5/6 yrs
//   rvMax 1.1, rvDays 10 +14,985 exTop10 +8,800  PF 1.43  6/6 yrs
// Robust, not a tuned spike: all 60 cells of a 12-lookback x 5-threshold grid are positive and beat
// baseline exTop10 (net +7,500..+14,985). Holds out of sample WITHIN the 5yr: fit-era 2021-23
// +5,999 (PF 1.34) and test-era 2024-26 +8,986 (PF 1.54) at these defaults. Slippage-flat.
// Mechanism: keeps ~62% of the "reached +70" edge bucket while cutting ~43% of the 8-70 popped-only
// weakness -- it thins the loser bucket faster than the edge bucket, NOT a winner-cutter.
//
// HOLDOUT-CONFIRMED (2026-08-20) -- gate now ON by default at rvMax 1.05. Four independent tests:
//   temporal split (fit 2021-23 -> chose 1.05, test 2024-26): +8,146 vs base +4,897, exTop10 -1,560
//     -> +2,071, 3/3 yrs. Reversed split (fit 2024-26, test 2021-23): +2,925 delta.
//   walk-forward (threshold refit each year from prior years only): +4,684 total, 5/5 yrs positive.
//   random control: 200 random day-subsets at the same 58% keep rate -- real beats ALL 200, p=0.000.
// Survives where the options/term-structure router died because rel-vol is a RATIO to its own
// trailing mean, so it self-normalizes: yearly mean 1.000-1.041, fire rate 48-62% across 6 years.
// Removed-trade W/L is correctly signed: removed bucket avg -12.5 pts/trade (it deletes losers).
//
// FRESH FORWARD BLOCK (Databento pull, 2026-06-24..08-19, 38 trades -- below the 50-trade floor,
// so SUGGESTIVE not confirmatory): baseline -2,994, filtered -797, delta +2,197; removed bucket
// -146/trade. Note ORB itself had its worst month on record in 2026-07 (WR 27.3%); the gate cut
// that month's loss by 73%. Surrounding months are normal (~52% WR), so this reads as one bad
// month, not decay -- but 2026-07 is worth watching.
//=============================
useRvGate = input.bool(true, "Rel-vol gate: only trade LOW opening-range-volume days", group="Rel-vol gate")
rvMax     = input.float(1.05, "Max rel-vol to take the break (OR vol / prior-days mean)", minval=0.1, step=0.05, group="Rel-vol gate")
rvDays    = input.int(10,   "Rel-vol baseline lookback (ACTIVE days, past-only)", minval=2, maxval=90, group="Rel-vol gate")

useCvdGate = input.bool(false, "CVD gate: skip breaks with trailing-CVD against them", group="CVD gate")
cvdWindow  = input.int(30,   "Trailing CVD window (bars = minutes on 1-min chart)", minval=1, maxval=120, group="CVD gate")
cvdThresh  = input.float(0.0, "Reject only if against-flow magnitude exceeds this (0 = sign gate)", minval=0.0, step=100.0, group="CVD gate")
cvdLtf     = input.timeframe("1S", "Lower timeframe for up/down volume classification", group="CVD gate")

//=============================
// Inputs -- exits (exitMode picks one). The docs flag exit choice as the whole game; sweep it.
//   0 = TRAIL  : trailing stop trailPts off best price since entry (let the day run)
//   1 = FIXED  : fixed take-profit tpPts / fixed stop slPts
//   2 = ORMULT : TP = tpMult * OR width, SL = other side of the OR (slMult * OR width)
//   3 = HOLD   : pure session-hold, flat at EOD, no stop (upper bound on the move)
//=============================
exitMode = input.int(0, "Exit mode (0=trail 1=fixed 2=OR-mult 3=EOD-hold)", minval=0, maxval=3, group="Exit")
trailPts = input.float(150.0, "TRAIL: trailing stop distance (pts)", minval=1.0, step=5.0, group="Exit")
tpPts    = input.float(120.0, "FIXED: take-profit (pts)",  minval=1.0, step=5.0, group="Exit")
slPts    = input.float(80.0,  "FIXED: stop-loss (pts)",    minval=1.0, step=5.0, group="Exit")
tpMult   = input.float(1.0,   "ORMULT: TP = this * OR width", minval=0.1, step=0.1, group="Exit")
slMult   = input.float(1.0,   "ORMULT: SL = this * OR width (other side of OR)", minval=0.1, step=0.1, group="Exit")

//=============================
// Inputs -- CATASTROPHIC STOP (independent overlay, composes with ANY exit mode). A per-trade stop
// at catMult * (trailing 14-day daily ATR) from entry. Volatility-scaled so it means the same thing
// in a hot year and a calm one -- a FIXED-point stop does NOT (validated: fixed stops chop runners;
// a wide k*ATR stop trims only the true disaster days). On EOD-hold this converts "ride to the
// close" into "ride to the close UNLESS price runs catMult*ATR against you first". Default ON at
// 1.5x: fires ~8 times in 5yr, improves net AND shrinks the worst-10 tail (Test A).
//=============================
useCatStop = input.bool(true, "Catastrophic stop: cap loss at catMult * trailing daily-ATR", group="Cat stop")
catMult    = input.float(1.5, "Cat stop distance = this * 14-day daily ATR (pts)", minval=0.25, step=0.25, group="Cat stop")
atrDays    = input.int(14,   "Daily-ATR lookback (days, trailing/past-only)", minval=1, maxval=60, group="Cat stop")

//=============================
// SESSION windows -- computed in Chicago minutes-since-midnight, identical to the other ports.
// (LDN = CT + 6h, shown for the London chart.)
//   RTH open  : 510 (08:30 CT = 14:30 LDN)
//   eodClose  : 900..960 (15:00-16:00 CT = 21:00-22:00 LDN)
//=============================
_ctMin     = hour(time, "America/Chicago") * 60 + minute(time, "America/Chicago")
rthOpenMin = 510   // 08:30 CT
_minSinceOpen = _ctMin - rthOpenMin
// HOLIDAY / WEEKEND / EARLY-CLOSE gap: a real session break shows up as a >60min jump between bars.
_gapEdge   = (time - time[1]) / 60000.0 > 60
eodClosed  = _ctMin >= 900 and _ctMin < 960
// Are we inside the opening-range accumulation window (open .. open+orMinutes)?
bool inORWindow = _minSinceOpen >= 0 and _minSinceOpen < orMinutes
// Are we inside the window where a break may be TAKEN (open+orMinutes .. open+breakEndMin)?
bool inBreakWindow = _minSinceOpen >= orMinutes and _minSinceOpen < breakEndMin
// A NEW day resets the OR: the first bar at/after the RTH open, or any bar after a session gap.
bool newDay = (_minSinceOpen == 0) or (_minSinceOpen >= 0 and _minSinceOpen[1] < 0) or _gapEdge

//=============================
// OPENING-RANGE accumulation. Track high/low across the OR window; freeze at window end. Reset each
// day. orReady flips true once the OR window has fully passed (we have a complete box to break).
//=============================
var float orHigh   = na
var float orLow    = na
var bool  orReady  = false
var bool  tookLong = false   // one long / one short per day
var bool  tookShort = false

if newDay
    orHigh    := na
    orLow     := na
    orReady   := false
    tookLong  := false
    tookShort := false

if inORWindow
    orHigh := na(orHigh) ? high : math.max(orHigh, high)
    orLow  := na(orLow)  ? low  : math.min(orLow,  low)

// The bar that first steps PAST the OR window freezes the box and marks it ready.
if _minSinceOpen >= orMinutes and not orReady and not na(orHigh)
    orReady := true

float orWidth = (na(orHigh) or na(orLow)) ? na : orHigh - orLow

//=============================
// TRAILING DAILY ATR (past-only). Accumulate the running day's high/low; at each new-day boundary
// push the COMPLETED day's range into a rolling buffer and set curDayATR = mean of the last atrDays
// completed ranges. curDayATR is therefore fixed for the whole day and uses only PAST days (no
// lookahead), matching backtest/orb_bt.py daily_atr exactly. na until atrDays full days have passed.
//=============================
var float dayHi     = na
var float dayLo     = na
var float curDayATR = na
var array<float> dayRanges = array.new<float>(0)

if newDay
    // finalize the day that just ended (dayHi/dayLo hold its full range from the prior bars)
    if not na(dayHi) and not na(dayLo)
        array.push(dayRanges, dayHi - dayLo)
        if array.size(dayRanges) > atrDays
            array.shift(dayRanges)                    // keep only the last atrDays completed ranges
    curDayATR := array.size(dayRanges) >= atrDays ? array.avg(dayRanges) : na
    dayHi := high
    dayLo := low
else
    dayHi := na(dayHi) ? high : math.max(dayHi, high)
    dayLo := na(dayLo) ? low  : math.min(dayLo,  low)

//=============================
// OPENING-RANGE RELATIVE VOLUME (past-only). Accumulate this day's OR-window volume; at the new-day
// boundary push the COMPLETED day's OR volume into a rolling buffer of the last rvDays ACTIVE days,
// then rv = today's OR volume / mean(buffer).
//
// "ACTIVE days" matters: weekend/holiday rows carry zero OR volume. Counting them as history drags
// the baseline toward zero and inflates rv on every real day, so only days with OR volume > 0 are
// pushed. (The first port of this returned zero trades at every threshold for exactly that reason.)
//
// Causality: the buffer holds only COMPLETED prior days, and today's own OR volume is fully known by
// the time the break window opens (the OR window has closed), so the gate reads no future data.
// curOrRelVol is fixed for the whole day. na until rvDays active days have accumulated.
//=============================
var float orVolAccum  = na    // this day's OR-window volume, accumulating
var float lastOrVol   = na    // the completed day's OR volume, pushed at the next new-day edge
var float curOrRelVol = na
var array<float> orVolHist = array.new<float>(0)

if newDay
    if not na(lastOrVol) and lastOrVol > 0
        array.push(orVolHist, lastOrVol)
        if array.size(orVolHist) > rvDays
            array.shift(orVolHist)                    // keep only the last rvDays ACTIVE days
    orVolAccum  := 0.0
    lastOrVol   := na
    curOrRelVol := na          // must reset, else a day with no baseline inherits yesterday's ratio

if inORWindow
    orVolAccum := nz(orVolAccum) + volume
    lastOrVol  := orVolAccum

// Freeze the ratio once the OR window has closed and a full baseline exists.
if _minSinceOpen >= orMinutes and array.size(orVolHist) >= rvDays and nz(orVolAccum) > 0
    curOrRelVol := orVolAccum / array.avg(orVolHist)

//=============================
// SLOPE into the break (simple net slope over slopeLen bars, pts/bar). Positive = rising.
//=============================
float breakSlope = (close - close[slopeLen]) / slopeLen

//=============================
// TRAILING CVD (aggressor-based order flow). For this bar, request the lower-timeframe (seconds)
// bars and sign each one's volume by its own direction (close>open = buying, close<open = selling) --
// this is TradingView's up/down-volume classification, the real aggressor delta available with a CME
// real-time feed. barDelta = this 1-min bar's net delta; trailCvd = rolling sum over cvdWindow bars.
// Only computed when the gate is on (request.security_lower_tf is not free). Causal: seconds bars are
// within the current bar, and math.sum uses only past+current bars.
//=============================
_udVol() =>
    close > open ? volume : close < open ? -volume : 0.0
// request.security_lower_tf must be called unconditionally at the top scope (not inside a ternary).
// It returns an array of the per-LTF-bar signed volume; array.sum collapses it to this bar's delta.
// na/empty (missing LTF data, last realtime bar) -> nz() folds it to 0 so the rolling sum survives.
array<float> _udArr = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, cvdLtf, _udVol())
float barDelta  = array.size(_udArr) > 0 ? array.sum(_udArr) : 0.0
float trailCvd  = useCvdGate ? math.sum(barDelta, cvdWindow) : na

//=============================
// BREAK signals. Long = first close beyond OR-high+buffer inside the break window; short = mirror.
// Gated by: orReady, break window, side toggle, one-per-day, OR-size filter, slope router.
//=============================
bool orSizeOK = orMinPts <= 0.0 or (not na(orWidth) and orWidth >= orMinPts)
// CVD gate: a LONG break is rejected if trailing-CVD runs against it (negative) by more than thresh;
// SHORT break rejected if trailing-CVD is positive by more than thresh. When the gate is off, both
// pass. thresh=0 makes it a plain sign gate.
bool cvdLongOK  = not useCvdGate or (not na(trailCvd) and trailCvd >= -cvdThresh)
bool cvdShortOK = not useCvdGate or (not na(trailCvd) and trailCvd <=  cvdThresh)
// REL-VOL gate: skip the whole day unless its OR volume is low vs its own recent baseline. Applies
// to both sides equally (it is a DAY filter, not a side filter). Days without a full baseline
// (curOrRelVol na -- the first rvDays of the chart) are SKIPPED, matching the port.
bool rvOK = not useRvGate or (not na(curOrRelVol) and curOrRelVol <= rvMax)
bool longBreak  = orReady and inBreakWindow and enableLong  and not tookLong  and orSizeOK and cvdLongOK and rvOK and
     not na(orHigh) and close > orHigh + breakBuf and
     (not useSlopeRouter or breakSlope >=  slopeMinPB)
bool shortBreak = orReady and inBreakWindow and enableShort and not tookShort and orSizeOK and cvdShortOK and rvOK and
     not na(orLow) and close < orLow - breakBuf and
     (not useSlopeRouter or breakSlope <= -slopeMinPB)

//=============================
// TRADE MANAGEMENT -- self-tracked position state (same scheme as slope_touch_fade: do NOT gate on
// strategy.position_size, which lags a bar under process_orders_on_close). tradeDir is our truth.
//=============================
var int   tradeDir       = 0     // +1 long, -1 short, 0 flat
var float entryPrice     = na
var float initialStop    = na    // fixed / OR-mult stop level
var float tpLevel        = na    // fixed / OR-mult take-profit level
var float catStop        = na    // catastrophic stop level (frozen at entry from entry-day ATR)
var float bestSinceEntry = na    // trail anchor: highest high (long) / lowest low (short)
// ---- alert / webhook state ----
var int    tradeSeq    = 0
var string tradeId     = ""
var string exitReason  = ""
var int    exitedDir   = 0
var string exitTradeId = ""

// 24-bit hash + seq suffix -> a stable id shared by a trade's entry and exit alerts.
makeTradeId(seq) =>
    _t  = int(time / 1000) % 1000000
    _px = int(close * 100) % 100000
    _h  = (_t * 131 + seq * 7919 + _px * 31) % 16777216
    _h := (_h * 2654435761) % 16777216
    _h := (_h + seq * 11400714819323) % 16777216
    _h := int(_h % 16777216)
    _hex = ""
    _digits = "0123456789abcdef"
    _v = _h
    for _i = 0 to 5
        _nib = int(_v % 16)
        _hex := str.substring(_digits, _nib, _nib + 1) + _hex
        _v := math.floor(_v / 16)
    _hex + "-" + str.tostring(seq)

bool flat = tradeDir == 0

// ---- ENTRIES (flat only) ----
// tookEntryLong/Short mark an ACTUAL fill this bar (a break signal alone is NOT a trade -- the
// entry is gated on `flat`, so a long break that fires while already short is ignored). The entry
// triangles plot from THESE, not from longBreak/shortBreak, so no phantom triangle prints for a
// break that did not result in a trade (e.g. a green "L" at the OR high while short from earlier).
bool tookEntryLong  = false
bool tookEntryShort = false
if flat
    if longBreak
        strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
        tookEntryLong  := true
        tradeDir       := 1
        entryPrice     := close
        tookLong       := true
        bestSinceEntry := high
        // initial stop + TP by exit mode:
        if exitMode == 1
            initialStop := close - slPts
            tpLevel     := close + tpPts
        else if exitMode == 2
            initialStop := orLow - slMult * orWidth       // other side of the OR
            tpLevel     := close + tpMult * orWidth
        else
            initialStop := na                              // trail (0) / hold (3): no fixed stop
            tpLevel     := na
        // catastrophic stop (frozen at entry from entry-day ATR); na if disabled or ATR not ready
        catStop := (useCatStop and not na(curDayATR)) ? close - catMult * curDayATR : na
        tradeSeq += 1
        tradeId := makeTradeId(tradeSeq)
    else if shortBreak
        strategy.entry("S", strategy.short)
        tookEntryShort := true
        tradeDir       := -1
        entryPrice     := close
        tookShort      := true
        bestSinceEntry := low
        if exitMode == 1
            initialStop := close + slPts
            tpLevel     := close - tpPts
        else if exitMode == 2
            initialStop := orHigh + slMult * orWidth
            tpLevel     := close - tpMult * orWidth
        else
            initialStop := na
            tpLevel     := na
        catStop := (useCatStop and not na(curDayATR)) ? close + catMult * curDayATR : na
        tradeSeq += 1
        tradeId := makeTradeId(tradeSeq)

// ---- MANAGE OPEN POSITION (driven by tradeDir; runs on entry bar and every bar after) ----
// exitMode: 0=trail off best, 1=fixed stop+TP, 2=OR-mult stop+TP, 3=pure EOD hold (no stop/TP).
float stopLevel     = na
float trailStopLine = na
string stopKind     = na
if tradeDir > 0
    bestSinceEntry := math.max(bestSinceEntry, high)
    if exitMode == 0
        trailStopLine := bestSinceEntry - trailPts
        stopLevel := trailStopLine
        stopKind  := "trail"
    else if exitMode == 1 or exitMode == 2
        stopLevel := initialStop
        stopKind  := exitMode == 2 ? "ormult" : "fixed"
    // catastrophic stop binds if it is TIGHTER (higher, for a long) than the mode stop -- and it
    // applies alone when the mode has none (EOD-hold). "cat" only labels the exit if it is binding.
    if not na(catStop) and (na(stopLevel) or catStop > stopLevel)
        stopLevel := catStop
        stopKind  := "cat"
    if not na(stopLevel) or not na(tpLevel)
        strategy.exit("L-exit", from_entry="L", stop=stopLevel, limit=tpLevel, comment=stopKind)
else if tradeDir < 0
    bestSinceEntry := math.min(bestSinceEntry, low)
    if exitMode == 0
        trailStopLine := bestSinceEntry + trailPts
        stopLevel := trailStopLine
        stopKind  := "trail"
    else if exitMode == 1 or exitMode == 2
        stopLevel := initialStop
        stopKind  := exitMode == 2 ? "ormult" : "fixed"
    if not na(catStop) and (na(stopLevel) or catStop < stopLevel)
        stopLevel := catStop
        stopKind  := "cat"
    if not na(stopLevel) or not na(tpLevel)
        strategy.exit("S-exit", from_entry="S", stop=stopLevel, limit=tpLevel, comment=stopKind)

// ---- SESSION FLATTEN (EOD / holiday gap) ----
bool sessionFlat = eodClosed or _gapEdge
if sessionFlat and tradeDir != 0
    strategy.close_all(comment="session")
    exitReason  := "session"
    exitedDir   := tradeDir
    exitTradeId := tradeId
    tradeDir := 0

// ---- SYNC tradeDir when the BROKER closed us out (a stop or TP filled) ----
if tradeDir != 0 and strategy.position_size == 0 and bar_index > 0 and strategy.position_size[1] != 0
    exitReason  := na(stopKind) ? "exit" : stopKind
    exitedDir   := tradeDir
    exitTradeId := tradeId
    tradeDir := 0

// reset per-trade state only when truly flat by OUR tracking
if tradeDir == 0
    entryPrice     := na
    initialStop    := na
    tpLevel        := na
    catStop        := na
    bestSinceEntry := na

//=============================
// Visuals -- OR box edges + break levels + active stop + entry triangles
//=============================
// OR box (only draw once the box is complete). Grey while forming, solid once ready.
plot(orReady ? orHigh : na, "OR high", color=color.new(color.teal, 0),  style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)
plot(orReady ? orLow  : na, "OR low",  color=color.new(color.teal, 0),  style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)
// break trigger levels (OR edge +/- buffer)
plot(orReady ? orHigh + breakBuf : na, "break-up level",   color=color.new(color.teal, 60), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)
plot(orReady ? orLow  - breakBuf : na, "break-down level", color=color.new(color.teal, 60), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)
// active stop, colored by side: FUCHSIA (below) = long stop, ORANGE (above) = short stop
plot(tradeDir > 0 ? stopLevel : na, "long stop",  color=color.new(color.fuchsia, 0), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
plot(tradeDir < 0 ? stopLevel : na, "short stop", color=color.new(color.orange,  0), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=2)
// take-profit (fixed / OR-mult modes)
plot(tradeDir != 0 and not na(tpLevel) ? tpLevel : na, "take-profit", color=color.new(color.yellow, 0), style=plot.style_linebr, linewidth=1)

// Entry triangles (trade color). Plot ACTUAL fills (tookEntryLong/Short), not raw break signals --
// a break that fires while already in a trade is ignored and must not print a phantom triangle.
plotshape(tookEntryLong,  "LONG entry",  shape.triangleup,   location.belowbar, color=color.new(color.lime, 0), size=size.small, text="L")
plotshape(tookEntryShort, "SHORT entry", shape.triangledown, location.abovebar, color=color.new(color.red,  0), size=size.small, text="S")

//=============================
// Version label -- bottom-right
//=============================
var table cityTable = table.new(position.bottom_right, 1, 1,
     bgcolor      = color.new(color.black, 20),
     border_width = 1,
     border_color = color.new(color.gray, 50))
if barstate.islast
    table.cell(cityTable, 0, 0, "Sapporo", text_color=color.yellow, text_size=size.small, bgcolor=color.new(color.navy, 10))

//=============================
// PARAM + EVENT columns (self-documenting export). Read the P_ columns before interpreting a chart.
//=============================
plot(orMinutes,   "P_orMinutes",   color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(breakEndMin, "P_breakEndMin", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(breakBuf,    "P_breakBuf",    color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(orMinPts,    "P_orMinPts",    color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(useSlopeRouter ? 1 : 0, "P_useSlopeRouter", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(slopeLen,    "P_slopeLen",    color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(slopeMinPB,  "P_slopeMinPB",  color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(exitMode,    "P_exitMode",    color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(trailPts,    "P_trailPts",    color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(tpPts,       "P_tpPts",       color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(slPts,       "P_slPts",       color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(tpMult,      "P_tpMult",      color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(slMult,      "P_slMult",      color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(useCatStop ? 1 : 0, "P_useCatStop", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(catMult,     "P_catMult",     color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(atrDays,     "P_atrDays",     color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(useRvGate ? 1 : 0, "P_useRvGate", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(rvMax,       "P_rvMax",      color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(rvDays,      "P_rvDays",     color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(useCvdGate ? 1 : 0, "P_useCvdGate", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(cvdWindow,   "P_cvdWindow",   color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(cvdThresh,   "P_cvdThresh",   color=na, display=display.data_window)

plot(orWidth,     "OR width (pts)",  color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(breakSlope,  "slope into break", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(trailCvd,    "trailing CVD",     color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(curDayATR,   "daily ATR (pts)",  color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(orVolAccum,  "OR volume",        color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(curOrRelVol, "OR rel-vol",       color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(catStop,     "cat stop lvl",     color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(stopLevel,   "active stop lvl",  color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(tookEntryLong  ?  1 : na, "EVT_long_entry",  color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot(tookEntryShort ? -1 : na, "EVT_short_entry", color=na, display=display.data_window)
plot((tookEntryLong or tookEntryShort) ? close : na, "EVT_entry_px", color=na, display=display.data_window)

//=============================
// Alerts -- JSON payloads for webhook REST API (same scheme as slope_touch_fade).
// In the TradingView alert dialog: paste your webhook URL, set message to {{alert_message}}.
//=============================
// Entry payload carries only what a webhook needs to execute: side, id, fill price, and the
// protective levels the strategy actually placed. sl/tp/sl_pts are the fixed / OR-mult stop+target;
// in TRAIL and EOD-HOLD modes there is no resting protective order, so they emit JSON null.
_slStr(v) => na(v) ? "null" : str.tostring(v, "0.00")

// EXIT alert FIRST (so a same-bar flip emits the close before any new entry). reason =
// session/stop/tp/trail/exit. Uses exitTradeId (id of the trade that closed).
bool exitFired = (tradeDir == 0 and tradeDir[1] != 0)
if exitFired
    _exitSide = exitedDir == 1 ? "long" : "short"
    alert('{"event":"exit","side":"' + _exitSide + '","id":"' + exitTradeId + '"' +
          ',"reason":"' + exitReason + '"' +
          ',"price":' + str.tostring(close, "0.00") +
          ',"symbol":"' + syminfo.ticker + '"' +
          ',"bar_time":"' + str.format_time(time, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", "Europe/London") + '"' +
          '}', alert.freq_once_per_bar)

if tradeDir == 1 and tradeDir[1] == 0
    alert('{"event":"entry","side":"long","id":"' + tradeId + '","price":' + str.tostring(close, "0.00") +
          ',"sl":' + _slStr(initialStop) +
          ',"tp":' + _slStr(tpLevel) +
          ',"sl_pts":' + (na(initialStop) ? "null" : str.tostring(math.abs(entryPrice - initialStop), "0.00")) +
          ',"symbol":"' + syminfo.ticker + '"' +
          ',"bar_time":"' + str.format_time(time, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", "Europe/London") + '"' +
          '}', alert.freq_once_per_bar)

if tradeDir == -1 and tradeDir[1] == 0
    alert('{"event":"entry","side":"short","id":"' + tradeId + '","price":' + str.tostring(close, "0.00") +
          ',"sl":' + _slStr(initialStop) +
          ',"tp":' + _slStr(tpLevel) +
          ',"sl_pts":' + (na(initialStop) ? "null" : str.tostring(math.abs(entryPrice - initialStop), "0.00")) +
          ',"symbol":"' + syminfo.ticker + '"' +
          ',"bar_time":"' + str.format_time(time, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", "Europe/London") + '"' +
          '}', alert.freq_once_per_bar)
